A||N||2||Seanh||Head/Lower Manifold not matching up correctly!||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||03-16-2001||09:35 PM||||I have the heads on, and put the lower manifold in last night. I couldnt help but notice how they dont match up very well. The heads seem to sit up more then the manifold. I am sure I torqued down the heads correctly and accuratly. I particularly notice them not matching up where the valve cover gasket goes on, where the head meets the manifold. I talked to a mechanic and he said this was normal. He said to finish the car, drive about a week, and remove the mid manifold and retorque the lower manifold bolts and I should be fine. Is that correct? He said they don't match up because the new head gaskets are stiffer and ticker and will hold the heads up a tad more. That the lower manifold will expand and contrant, and eventually form between the heads. I was just curious if he is feeding me a line of crap, because it sounds a liitle off, but I dont know. If I have a huge problem here, I am so sick of this car I am going to call a tow truck and have GM work on it, I can't take this anymore. Any ideas about whats happening? Thanks.<P>Also, all the gaskets are new. Head gaskets and lower intake manifold gaskets.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||03-16-2001||10:37 PM||||I have noticed that happening to with some engines. When I find the fit to be abnormal (I love that word!), I run a bead of RTV on the mating surfaces and GENTLY set the intake on and let it set for cure and then torque it. (make sure to put some on the bolt threads-not too much!)<BR>If you want a good seal on the valve covers check that your set has the rubber gaskets and not the cork. They will conform to the uneven surfaces much better than the cork.<P>Luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||03-17-2001||06:53 AM||||I just went out to look at it again and I really dont think the matching is as far off as I first thought it was. But, the lower manifold gasket is sticking up a little, and that kinda makes it look mismatched. I am going to just cut off the gasket even with the the valve cover seal and call it good. I havent gotten the valve cover gaskets yet. I am doing that today. I bought a set from Napa and the only gasket it doesn't have is Fiero valve covers, figures. Oh well, it should be running later today, I hope. If I have the time, I might put some RVT on there and let it set-up for a while. I already did that with the black RTV on the edges of the lower manifold, but I didnt use more then it said to use. Thanks. Glad to know I dont have a huge problem here!||||reg||1
